Subject: [PATCH] vayu_wifi W25p: 256 TX slots, a 32-frame queue when the pool is full (the "no slot"
 drops at the TCP window's peak), and the in-flight cap from the CE4 source ring

Base: the merged W25o tree (/mnt/ramdisk/merge-all, 0060 applied; run 150920: 9987 frames sent,
9987 completed, status 0:9959 1:25 2:3, slots back to 0 in flight, but "drops: no slot 290").

Changes:
 - bsd/dev/vayu_wifi_scan.c: TX_SLOTS 64 -> 256 (a uint64_t[4] bitmap, all of it under tx_lock);
   the TX pool htt_pool_alloc()s 256 x 2048 = 512 KiB, the frag bank already has room for
   HTT_MAX_PENDING_TX (1056) entries.  The msdu id is the slot number, 0..255, well inside the
   16-bit field of htt_data_tx_desc_64.
 - the in-flight limit is min(256, CE4 source ring entries - 2): the HTC/HTT layer hands the CE4
   source ring size over in vayu_scan_ops.tx_ring (bsd/dev/vayu_wifi_htc_connect.c, from
   src_ring(VAYU_HTCC_HTT_TX_CE)), so the H2T ring can never run dry behind the pool.
 - a full pool is no longer a drop: tx_frame() returns -2 and bsd/dev/vayu_wifi_net.c puts the
   frame in a 32-frame queue (kalloc'd once, its own lock).  The HTT completion path kicks the
   queue as slots come free (vayu_net_tx_kick(), called from vayu_scan_htt_tx_compl() and once per
   100 ms from the station loop).  The interface's transmit callback accepts the frame in that
   case (true to ifnet) instead of dropping it, so TCP keeps its window.
 - the 10 s line now prints slots in flight/free of 256, the ring cap, the queue depth, and the
   queue counters are in vayu_net_summary ("queue N queued/M sent/K dropped (depth D)").

Expected: "no slot" stops growing (it now means "queued", and the queue drains within a
completion), the line reads "slots in flight 0..40, free 216..256 of 256 (ring cap 2046); queue 0",
and no "dropped" on en0 at the peak.

